# Everything here is either large, host-specific, or actively wrong inside a
# container. The build context is sent to the daemon in full on every build,
# so exclusions are a rebuild-speed concern, not just tidiness.

# 150 MB parquet. Excluding this alone is most of the build-context savings.
data/

# Host virtualenvs: large, and Linux wheels are not what Windows venvs hold.
.venv/
venv/

# The container gets its configuration from compose `environment:` entries.
# config.py calls load_dotenv(), which does NOT override variables already
# set in the environment -- but that only helps if this file never reaches
# the image. The host .env points at localhost:9092 and localhost:5433, both
# unreachable from inside a container, and baking it in would produce a
# confusing connection failure instead of a clear one.
.env

# Build, test and tooling output
.git/
.github/
.idea/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
graphify-out/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Local-only instructions, deliberately gitignored
CLAUDE.md
